# DOMAIN 3 — ECONOMIC FRACTURE SIGNALS

## Purpose of this domain
Detect quiet economic shifts that constrain civilians and households before headlines — especially changes that tighten options, shorten timelines, or alter rules around access to money, services, or stability.

This domain is not about markets.  
It’s about pressure propagation.

---

## 3.1 What still belongs (validated)

These remain core:
- Treasury / bond market stress
- Currency and trade realignment
- Banking instability
- Capital controls / payment restrictions
- Cost-of-living shocks

Structure holds.

---

## 3.2 What changed (re-baseline)

### A. Fracture now shows up as friction, not collapse

Less “crash,” more:
- delayed payments  
- stricter eligibility  
- slower processing  
- narrower grace windows  
- “temporary” restrictions that linger  

So we stop watching for fireworks and start watching for drag.

---

### B. Households feel it before systems admit it

A recurring pattern:
> Households encounter constraint before institutions acknowledge stress.

Signals tied to benefits, banking access, utilities, housing, and transportation carry higher practical weight than abstract macro indicators.

---

## 3.3 Triggers

### 🔴 ALERT-ELIGIBLE (rare, proximity-based)

These only alert if they shorten reaction time or remove options.

| Trigger | P | I | O | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Restrictions on cash access or withdrawals | L | H | M | Any form, even “temporary” |
| Payment system outages affecting essentials | M | H | H | Food, rent, utilities |
| Sudden benefits interruption or rule change | M | H | M | Households are hit first |
| Emergency economic measures tied to security | L | H | M | Watch coupling |
| Rapid cost spikes in essentials (local) | M | M | H | Food, fuel, utilities |

**Alert rule:**  
👉 Must affect the relevant local area and reduce options within days, not months.

---

### 🟡 LOG-ONLY (primary function of this domain)

Most of Domain 3 lives here.

| Trigger | P | I | O | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Treasury or bond market stress signals | M | H | M | Early but abstract |
| Foreign sell-off of sovereign debt | M | M | M | Contextual |
| Trade settlement shifts (e.g., BRICS) | M | M | M | Long arc |
| Bank tightening / credit contraction | H | M | H | Shows up quietly |
| Insurance withdrawal from regions | M | M | M | Housing + risk |
| Utility pricing or service changes | M | M | H | Household impact |
| Corporate insolvency clusters | M | M | M | Employment lag |

Purpose: pattern + lead time, not daily anxiety.

---

### 🔵 SUSPEND / LOW-FOCUS

Deprioritize:
- hyperinflation speculation  
- “reserve currency collapse” narratives  
- crypto-as-savior cycles  
- day-to-day market volatility  

Reactivation only if:
- policy response follows  
- access restrictions appear  
- essential services are affected  

---

## 3.4 Household Impact Override (Domain 3)

Immediate escalation only if economic changes affect:
- food access (benefits, school meals, pricing shocks)  
- housing stability or utilities  
- healthcare access or coverage  
- transportation required for school, work, or care  

Markets can burn quietly.  
Households cannot.

---

## 3.5 Plateau rule (important here)

Domain 3 enters plateau if:
- no access restrictions  
- benefits remain stable  
- utilities remain uninterrupted  
- pricing changes remain gradual  

Plateau = weekly synthesis only.  
No daily scanning.
